WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Case File 02, Drug-Free Schizophrenia
Research.

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:06.959
Highly vulnerable patients were taken off effective
antipsychotic medications to test a placebo.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.119
This violates the Helsinki requirement to test
against the best proven standard of care,

4
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:17.380
exploiting patients with fluctuating capacity
and creating severe conflicts of interest.

5
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.779
Real-world scientific environments are riddled
with these exact types of power imbalances and

6
00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.700
conflicting interests.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.540
Objective and forcible ethical frameworks
are the only reliable defense against harm.

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.299
Our final stress test addresses an extreme
existential risk.

9
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.179
This photograph captures citizens during
the 1918 influenza pandemic, a

10
00:00:37.179 --> 00:00:38.859
virus that killed tens of millions.

11
00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:44.839
Case File 03 examines the 2005 reconstruction
of the 1918 Spanish flu virus.

12
00:00:44.839 --> 00:00:49.559
This is a textbook example of dual-use
research of concern.

13
00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:55.539
Research intended for medical benefit that could
easily be misapplied for catastrophic harm,

14
00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.619
carrying immense biosafety containment
risks.

15
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.679
This forces a critical question of
distributed responsibility.

16
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.239
Does the freedom of scientific inquiry
justify the creation of a hyperlethal weapon?

17
00:01:08.239 --> 00:01:11.760
And who bears the moral weight of that
sequence being published?

18
00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.080
The scientists, the funders, or the

19
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:15.980
journals?

20
00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.659
Navigating these questions requires a
reliable system of orientation, the

21
00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:22.260
compass of the ethical researcher.

22
00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:26.179
The four cardinal points bring together
everything we've covered.

23
00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:30.659
Rigorous integrity of methods, unwavering
respect for subjects,

24
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:35.239
broad societal accountability, and the
protected freedom of inquiry.

25
00:01:35.239 --> 00:01:40.320
Ultimately, this active framework is the
vital foundation that ensures

26
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.659
scientific progress remains a valid,
deeply trusted,

27
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.599
and fundamentally humane pursuit for
everyone.
